<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>InputLeap</displayName>
  <description>Policies for InputLeap keyboard and mouse sharing.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="InputLeap">InputLeap</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_InputLeap">Versions of InputLeap that support policies</string>

      <string id="ClipboardSharing">Allow clipboard sharing</string>
      <string id="ClipboardSharing_Explain">Controls whether text and images copied on one computer can be pasted on the other.

If you disable this policy, clipboard contents are never sent or received, whatever the user or the server configuration chooses.

If you enable this policy or do not configure it, users decide.</string>

      <string id="FileTransfer">Allow file transfer</string>
      <string id="FileTransfer_Explain">Controls whether files can be transferred between computers by dragging and dropping them across screens.

If you disable this policy, file transfer is turned off and cannot be turned on.

If you enable this policy or do not configure it, users decide.</string>

      <string id="RequireEncryption">Require encryption</string>
      <string id="RequireEncryption_Explain">Requires TLS encryption for all connections, so that keystrokes, mouse movement and clipboard contents are never sent unencrypted.

If you enable this policy, encryption is always on and users cannot turn it off.

If you disable this policy or do not configure it, users decide. Encryption is on by default.</string>

      <string id="AllowedConnectionModes">Allowed connection modes</string>
      <string id="AllowedConnectionModes_Explain">Controls how computers may connect to each other: over the network (Wi-Fi or Ethernet), over Bluetooth, or both.

If you enable this policy, only the selected modes can be used. Connections using another mode are refused.

If you disable this policy or do not configure it, both modes are allowed.</string>
      <string id="AllowedConnectionModes_Both">Network and Bluetooth</string>
      <string id="AllowedConnectionModes_Network">Network only</string>
      <string id="AllowedConnectionModes_Bluetooth">Bluetooth only</string>

      <string id="LockSettings">Prevent changes to settings</string>
      <string id="LockSettings_Explain">Prevents users from changing InputLeap's settings (screen name, port, network interface, encryption, logging and similar).

If you enable this policy, the settings window is read-only.

If you disable this policy or do not configure it, users can change settings.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="AllowedConnectionModes">
        <dropdownList refId="AllowedConnectionModes_Enum" defaultItem="0">Allowed modes:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
